[{"id":"collector-handbook-00","source":"collector-handbook.txt","index":0,"section":"DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS COLLECTOR HANDBOOK","sections":["DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS COLLECTOR HANDBOOK","1. WELCOME TO THE POND","2. SETTING UP YOUR COLLECTION","2. SETTING UP YOUR COLLECTION › 2.1 Start with the catalog","2. SETTING UP YOUR COLLECTION › 2.2 Add your cards carefully","2. SETTING UP YOUR COLLECTION › 2.3 A good routine"],"words":373,"overlapWords":0,"text":"DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS COLLECTOR HANDBOOK\n\nVersion: November 2026\n\nThis handbook is about collecting and trading well with Ducks on the Pond Cards. For button-by-button steps, see the User's Guide (users-guide.txt). For rules, see the Terms of Use (terms-of-use.txt) and the Customer Service Policy (customer-service-policy.txt). Words you may not know are explained in the Glossary (glossary.txt).\n\n1. WELCOME TO THE POND\n\nDucks on the Pond Cards is a shared notebook for sports card collectors. You keep a record of the cards you own, say which ones you would trade, list the cards you are hunting for, and the Application points you to collectors who have what you want.\n\nThe Application keeps records. It does not hold money, ship cards or check that a card is genuine. The cards, and the trust between collectors, are yours.\n\nThe name comes from baseball: \"ducks on the pond\" means runners on base, waiting to be brought home. Your wishlist is your ducks on the pond.\n\n2. SETTING UP YOUR COLLECTION\n\n2.1 Start with the catalog\n\nEvery card you own is a copy of a catalog variant. Before you add a card, check that its set, card and parallel are in the Catalog. If not, add them (User's Guide section 5). The catalog is shared, so:\n\n- Look through the Sets table before adding a set, to avoid duplicates. - Use the manufacturer's own names, for example \"Topps\" and \"Chrome\". - Enter the print run on numbered parallels. Without it, serial numbers cannot be checked. - If you spot a mistake you cannot fix, report it (Customer Service Policy section 8).\n\n2.2 Add your cards carefully\n\nYou cannot edit a copy's grade, serial or paid price after it is added, so check before you click \"Add card\":\n\n- The right variant: Base, Refractor, Gold Refractor and so on, and Auto or Relic where it applies. - The serial number exactly as stamped, without the print run. For 23/50, enter 23. - For a graded card, both the grading company and the grade, plus the cert number from the slab label. - What you paid and when. Your reports are only as good as these numbers.\n\nIf you make a mistake, delete the copy and add it again.","tokens":507,"embedding":[-0.06785045564174652,0.056674838066101074,-0.0739213079214096,-0.049665793776512146,0.0032483490649610758,0.031706638634204865,0.06382545083761215,0.032538529485464096,0.01316638570278883,-0.009107649326324463,0.03897881507873535,-0.053025390952825546,0.014282483607530594,-0.029420820996165276,-0.06944139301776886,-0.04397042095661163,-0.029440585523843765,0.012158391065895557,-0.027695395052433014,0.026860138401389122,0.03757929801940918,0.016529932618141174,-0.015137230977416039,0.047724440693855286,-0.05711090937256813,0.006815462838858366,-0.12551137804985046,0.03341761976480484,-0.10416847467422485,-0.039838697761297226,-0.03055013157427311,0.1153753474354744,0.07533618062734604,0.023030182346701622,0.019971875473856926,-0.048345766961574554,-0.04834536835551262,0.015629028901457787,0.006835385225713253,-0.06017162278294563,-0.02901300974190235,-0.05994876101613045,-0.07681106775999069,0.0589124821126461,-0.03972921520471573,0.01914372853934765,-0.05507800728082657,0.014933092519640923,-0.011567853391170502,0.09252194315195084,-0.03554113954305649,0.02028726041316986,-0.05815567448735237,0.01584130898118019,0.056892845779657364,0.10446176677942276,0.026623910292983055,-0.043205708265304565,-0.044093117117881775,-0.08123689889907837,0.017788328230381012,-0.03598065674304962,-0.06976442039012909,0.0183589905500412,0.00853054691106081,-