in a plastic case (a slab) by a grading company, which gives it a grade from 1 to 10. The Application supports PSA, BGS, SGC and CGC, in half-grade steps.\n\n3.2 What graders look at\n\n- Centering: how evenly the image sits within the borders. - Corners: sharp, or rounded and soft. - Edges: clean, or chipped and rough. - Surface: scratches, print lines, dents, stains.\n\n3.3 Describing a raw card honestly\n\nUse plain words in condition notes, and describe the worst flaw first. For example: \"Light whitening on the back top-left corner; front clean; centering about 60/40 left to right.\" Never call a raw card \"gem mint\" or give it a number grade of your own. A grade means a grading company's grade.\n\n3.4 Protecting your cards\n\n- Penny sleeve and top loader for raw cards of any value. - Keep cards away from sunlight, damp and heat. - Handle by the edges.\n\n4. TRADING WELL\n\n4.1 Before you offer\n\n- Turn on Tradeable only for cards you have in hand and would really part with. Collectors will make offers based on it. - Use public wants. They are how other collectors find you. - Set a minimum grade and a maximum price on wants, so matches are worth your time.","tokens":442,"embedding":[-0.12990252673625946,0.08257662504911423,-0.046970393508672714,-0.019401689991354942,-0.0004751434607896954,0.005558912176638842,-0.022321097552776337,0.12687885761260986,-0.025123201310634613,-0.006173384375870228,0.02361363172531128,-0.03808681294322014,0.016516009345650673,0.025020496919751167,-0.02655269205570221,-0.07247690856456757,0.02747546136379242,0.05810458958148956,-0.0655159056186676,0.04078920558094978,0.04662276804447174,-0.046781688928604126,-0.03294210135936737,0.01858549565076828,-0.03196929767727852,0.03925532475113869,-0.030742349103093147,0.011167907156050205,-0.04187582805752754,-0.056903090327978134,-0.027749869972467422,0.12381765991449356,0.08517821133136749,0.06353388726711273,0.007502860389649868,-0.04436124861240387,-0.006820709444582462,-0.00717820040