de\" fills in the collector and card for you. - Say in the message how you would like to exchange the cards, and how you will pack them. - Offer fair value. Recent sales of the same card and grade are a better guide than asking prices. - Do not be put off by a counteroffer. It is how trades get agreed.\n\n4.3 Exchanging the cards\n\n- Agree who sends first. For a first trade with someone, sending at the same time, or meeting at a card show, is common. - Pack cards in a sleeve and top loader, between card board, in a padded envelope or small box. Use tracked post for anything of value. - When the cards arrive, check the set, card number, parallel, serial, grade and cert number against the trade. - Only then click \"Complete (cards exchanged)\". Completing moves the records and cannot be undone by you.\n\n4.4 After the trade\n\nCards you receive arrive with Tradeable off and no paid price. Add notes, and turn Tradeable on if you want to offer them again.\n\n4.5 When something goes wrong\n\nTalk to your trading partner first. If you cannot sort it out within 7 days, contact support with the details listed in section 4 of the Customer Service Policy.\n\n5. SELLING\n\nThe Application does not handle sales, but it helps you keep track:\n\n- Enter a listed price to show a card in your For sale report. Other collectors cannot see listed prices. - Record the sale price and date with \"Mark sold\". The Sold report then shows your profit. - Arrange payment and delivery yourself, using a method that protects both sides.","tokens":413,"embedding":[-0.14501941204071045,0.044988952577114105,-0.08641558140516281,0.009356331080198288,-0.0519973523914814,0.0346987210214138,0.024166548624634743,0.07869210839271545,-0.010129991918802261,-0.011310011148452759,0.024388756603002548,-0.006927161943167448,-0.012697364203631878,-0.025358587503433228,0.006918593775480986,-0.03957539424300194,0.042138900607824326,0.007370629347860813,-0.05329052358865738,0.07596757262945175,0.02678367123007774